{% extends 'layout.twig' %}
{% block title %}{{ name }} – your Birthday Star{% endblock %}
{% block bodyclass %}page-result{% endblock %}
{% block content %}
<section class="reveal" aria-labelledby="star-name">
  <p class="reveal-intro">Born {{ r.birth|date('F j, Y') }} … you are {{ age_years|number_format(1) }} years old … searching {{ star_count|number_format }} nearby stars …</p>
  <div class="reveal-burst" aria-hidden="true"><span class="burst-star"></span></div>
  <p class="reveal-kicker">Your Birthday Star is</p>
  <h1 id="star-name" class="star-name">{{ name }}</h1>
  {% if hawaiian %}<p class="hawaiian-name">Hawaiian name: <strong lang="haw">{{ hawaiian.hawaiian }}</strong>{% if hawaiian.meaning %} <span class="hint">("{{ hawaiian.meaning }}")</span>{% endif %}</p>{% endif %}
  {% if designation != name %}<p class="designation">also called <strong>{{ designation }}</strong></p>{% endif %}
</section>

<section class="explain card">
  <h2>The light you see left it around when you were born</h2>
  <p class="big-number"><span>{{ star.distanceLy|number_format(1) }}</span> light years away</p>
  {% if r.isTooYoungForAnyStar %}
  <p>You are {{ age_years|number_format(1) }} years old, and that's so young that no other star's light has had time to make the whole trip in your lifetime! {{ name }} is one of the closest stars of all. Its light set off <strong>{{ star.distanceLy|number_format(1) }} years</strong> ago, before you were born, and the light leaving it today will arrive in about {{ (star.distanceLy - age_years)|round(0, 'ceil') }} years. Come back then!</p>
  {% else %}
  <p>You are about <strong>{{ age_years|number_format(1) }} years old</strong>. Light from {{ name }} takes about <strong>{{ star.distanceLy|number_format(1) }} years</strong> to reach Earth. So the starlight arriving in your eyes tonight <strong>set off around {{ r.lightLeftOn|date('F Y') }}</strong>, right around when you were born. It has been zooming through space your whole life!</p>
  {% endif %}
  <p class="aside">Light is the fastest thing there is: {{ light_speed_miles|number_format }} miles every second. But the trip is about <strong>{{ (miles / 1e12)|number_format(0) }} trillion miles</strong> long!</p>
</section>

<section class="facts" aria-label="Fun facts">
  <div class="fact card">
    <h3>How bright?</h3>
    <p>Magnitude {{ star.magnitude|number_format(1) }}: {{ facts.brightness }}</p>
    <p class="hint">In astronomy, smaller numbers mean brighter stars.</p>
  </div>
  {% if constellation %}
  <div class="fact card">
    <h3>Constellation</h3>
    <p>It's in <strong>{{ constellation }}</strong>{% if constellation_meaning %}, {{ constellation_meaning }}{% endif %}.</p>
  </div>
  {% endif %}
  <div class="fact card">
    <h3>Can I see it from Hawaiʻi?</h3>
    {% if not facts.ever_rises %}
    <p>Sadly, no. It's so far south that it never rises above the horizon at {{ facts.place }}.</p>
    {% else %}
      {% if facts.up_tonight %}
      <p><strong>Yes, it's up tonight!</strong> At 8:30 pm it is about {{ facts.tonight_altitude }}° above the horizon. Look toward the {{ facts.direction }}.</p>
      {% else %}
      <p>Not this evening. It's best seen in the evening around <strong>{{ facts.best_month }}</strong>, high in the {{ facts.direction }}ern sky (up to {{ facts.max_altitude }}°).</p>
      {% endif %}
      {% if not facts.naked_eye %}<p class="hint">You'll need binoculars or a telescope.</p>{% endif %}
    {% endif %}
  </div>
  {% if star.spectralType %}
  <div class="fact card">
    <h3>What kind of star?</h3>
    <p>Spectral type <strong>{{ star.spectralType }}</strong>.
    {% set t = star.spectralType|first|upper %}
    {% if t == 'O' or t == 'B' %}A hot, blue-white star, much hotter than our Sun!
    {% elseif t == 'A' %}A white star, hotter than our Sun.
    {% elseif t == 'F' %}A yellow-white star, a bit hotter than our Sun.
    {% elseif t == 'G' %}A yellow star, a lot like our Sun!
    {% elseif t == 'K' %}An orange star, a bit cooler than our Sun.
    {% elseif t == 'M' %}A red star, cooler than our Sun.
    {% elseif t == 'D' %}A white dwarf: the tiny, hot leftover core of an old star.
    {% endif %}</p>
  </div>
  {% endif %}
</section>

<section class="photo card" aria-labelledby="photo-h">
  <h2 id="photo-h">Your star, photographed by a real telescope</h2>
  {% if photo %}
  <figure class="photo-fig">
    <div class="photo-frame">
      <img src="{{ base }}/assets/survey/{{ photo.file }}" width="600" height="600" loading="lazy"
           alt="Telescope photo of the sky around {{ name }}, which is in the centre of the circle.">
      <svg class="photo-mark" viewBox="0 0 100 100" width="100%" height="100%" preserveAspectRatio="none" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><g class="photo-ring" fill="none" stroke="#ff8bd1" stroke-width="0.8"><circle cx="50" cy="50" r="9" fill="none"/><path d="M50 32v8M50 60v8M32 50h8M60 50h8" fill="none"/></g></svg>
      <span class="photo-label" aria-hidden="true">{{ name }}</span>
    </div>
    <figcaption>
      <p>{{ name }} is in the middle of the circle. This patch of sky is <strong>{{ photo.fov_words }}</strong>.
      {% if photo.pan_starrs %}It was taken by the <strong>Pan-STARRS</strong> telescope on top of <strong>Haleakalā, Maui</strong>, right here in Hawaiʻi!{% elseif photo.twomass %}It comes from <strong>2MASS</strong>, a survey that photographed the whole sky in <strong>infrared</strong> light, which our eyes can't see, so the colours are made up to show it.{% else %}It comes from the <strong>Digitized Sky Survey</strong>, made from big glass photographic plates taken by telescopes in California and Australia.{% endif %}</p>
      {% if star.magnitude < 4 %}
      <p class="hint">Why does it look like a big glowing blob? {{ name }} is so bright that its light floods the camera, spilling over and making spikes and halos. The star itself is really a tiny point!</p>
      {% else %}
      <p class="hint">Every dot is a star (and some fuzzy smudges are whole galaxies far beyond!). Bright stars look bigger only because their light spreads out in the camera.</p>
      {% endif %}
      <p class="credit">Image: {{ photo.credit }}. Field of view {{ photo.fov_deg }}°.</p>
    </figcaption>
  </figure>
  {% else %}
  <p class="photo-missing">We don't have a telescope photo of {{ name }} here yet, but you can find it on the sky chart below!</p>
  {% endif %}
</section>

<section class="chart-wrap card" aria-labelledby="chart-h">
  <h2 id="chart-h">Find it in the sky</h2>
  <p class="hint noprint">Drag to look around. Pinch, use the mouse wheel, or the + and − buttons to zoom. On larger screens, use the arrow buttons or click the chart and press the arrow keys.</p>
  <div class="chart-box">
    <canvas id="skychart" class="skychart" tabindex="0" role="img"
      aria-label="Star chart centred on {{ name }} in {{ constellation ?: 'the sky' }}"
      data-ra="{{ (star.raHours * 15)|round(4) }}" data-dec="{{ star.decDeg|round(4) }}" data-name="{{ name }}"
      data-stars="{{ base }}/assets/data/sky-stars.json" data-lines="{{ base }}/assets/data/constellations.lines.json" data-names="{{ base }}/assets/data/constellations.names.json" data-hawaiian="{{ base }}/assets/data/hawaiian-star-names.json"
      data-con="{{ star.constellation }}" data-con-name="{{ constellation }}" width="900" height="600"></canvas>
    <div class="chart-controls noprint">
      <div class="chart-dpad" role="group" aria-label="Pan the sky chart">
        <button type="button" class="btn-round" data-pan="up" aria-label="Pan up">↑</button>
        <button type="button" class="btn-round" data-pan="left" aria-label="Pan left">←</button>
        <button type="button" class="btn-round" data-pan="right" aria-label="Pan right">→</button>
        <button type="button" class="btn-round" data-pan="down" aria-label="Pan down">↓</button>
      </div>
      <div class="chart-zoom">
        <button type="button" class="btn-round" data-zoom="in" aria-label="Zoom in">+</button>
        <button type="button" class="btn-round" data-zoom="out" aria-label="Zoom out">−</button>
        <button type="button" class="btn-round" data-zoom="reset" aria-label="Centre on my star">◎</button>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
  <p class="coords">Sky coordinates (J2000): RA {{ (star.raHours)|number_format(3) }} h, Dec {{ star.decDeg|number_format(2) }}°</p>
</section>

<section class="actions noprint">
  <a class="btn btn-big" href="{{ base }}/{% if kiosk %}kiosk{% endif %}">Try another birthday ✦</a>
  {% if not kiosk %}<button type="button" class="btn" id="print-btn">Print my star</button>{% endif %}
</section>

<details class="inspire card noprint">
  <summary>How does this work? (and how you could do it too)</summary>
  <p>Astronomers measure star distances by watching each star shift a tiny bit as Earth goes around the Sun. That shift is called <em>parallax</em>. Satellites like <strong>Hipparcos</strong> and <strong>Gaia</strong> measured millions of stars this way.
  This website looks up how old you are, then searches a catalog of thousands of nearby stars for the one whose distance in light years best matches your age.</p>
  <p>Telescopes on <strong>Maunakea</strong>, right here on Hawaiʻi Island, study stars like yours every night. Scientists, engineers and computer programmers all work together there. Love space? Love puzzles? Love computers? There's a place for you in astronomy!</p>
</details>
<p class="print-only">{{ source }}. Find your own Birthday Star with Journey Through the Universe!</p>
{% endblock %}
